From d672aa32f698ddd24df6da12d69a17778fb0e4e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(vm): say which kind of arena exhaustion the warning
 is about

"the compressible VmRegion arena is exhausted" did not say whether the live
set outgrew the arena (raise SMASH_VM_GIB) or the arena is fragmented (a
larger one only postpones it). It now reports pages handed out, free pages
still in the map and the longest reusable run, and names the likely cause.

PageRunMap keeps a per-owner free-page count and reports the highest
non-empty size bin as a lower bound on its longest run.

Measured: a workload whose live set exceeds a 1 GiB arena reports "1023 of
1024 MiB handed out, 0 MiB free in 0-page runs or shorter" and points at
SMASH_VM_GIB. Suite 58/58.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
