+From 8ebfca0cf9c528209420f3797df93c63391ea4a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:55:39 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(slab): fall back to a direct mapping when the arena
+ is exhausted
+
+Reported on aarch64 (4 KiB pages): std::bad_alloc and "terminate called
+recursively" in full mode only; SMASH_LARGE_ONLY=1 worked. The latter is
+libstdc++ reporting a second thread reaching std::terminate while the first
+is in it: several threads got bad_alloc at once.
+
+Small objects live in slab spans carved from the VmRegion arena, and when
+the arena ran out Slab::allocateNewSpan returned nullptr; large allocations
+fall back to direct mmap, small ones had none. The arena runs out without a
+large live set because an empty span's pages stay with its (arena, size
+class): Slab::scavenge() has no callers. Reproduced with SMASH_VM_GIB=1:
+800 MiB of 64-byte objects, all freed, then 128-byte objects failed after
+173 MiB with the arena at 262143/262144 pages.
+
+A span now falls back to vm::mapPages; region-only steps (page states,
+release hook, cold counts, releasePages) are skipped for it via
+Slab::inRegion(), and emptying it uses the new vm::decommitOwnMapping(),
+since decommitPages() traps on addresses outside the arena. Its pages are
+not compressed; a one-time warning says so.
+
+Every full-mode allocation about to return nullptr now reports why
+(util/alloc_failure.h: path, size, alignment, errno, arena usage, VMA count
+against vm.max_map_count; rate-limited and allocation-free). It is what
+identified this failure.
+
+New test_small_arena_exhaustion: three 800 MiB phases of different size
+classes in a 1 GiB arena, every object's pattern verified; the previous
+library fails phase B at 173 MiB. 64 threads x 10 rounds with the arena
+exhausted: 2.56 M allocations, 0 nulls. Suite 54/54, unprivileged and root.
+
+Not done: returning empty spans to the arena. Spans are 1-8 pages by class
+and freed runs are not coalesced, so that alone would not have prevented
+this case.
+
