++Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(mmap): never track hugetlb mappings; re-enable both
++ disabled tests
++
++Two independent changes that together leave no test disabled.
++
++1. MAP_HUGETLB carve-out (test_hugepage_no_mprotect_storm, re-enabled).
++Under SMASH_TRACK_EXTERNAL=1 the mmap interposer registered every 4 KiB
++slice of an application MAP_HUGETLB mapping. hugetlb VMAs reject every
++4 KiB mprotect/madvise/MAP_FIXED, nothing records that a page is
++unmanageable, so the compressor retried every tick forever: 8192 failing
++page operations in 6 s for one 16 MiB mapping, with the slices holding the
++external-page budget. The filter is now isTrackableMapping(), which skips
++MAP_HUGETLB. mremap's flags cannot say MAP_HUGETLB and its interposer
++registered any moved or grown range, so a move re-registered the mapping;
++it now tracks a remapped range only if the source was tracked.
++Discriminators (strict test): skip removed -> 8192 failing ops; only the
++mremap gate removed -> 1024 (one moved 2 MiB mapping); both -> 0. Anonymous
++mappings grown by mremap are still tracked and compressed. A file-backed
++mapping grown by mremap stayed resident before the gate too, so no file
++mapping fix is claimed. The test now also moves one mapping with mremap.
++
++2. test_fault_cycle (re-enabled, plus test_fault_cycle_eager_reclaim).
++Disabled in June as "signal-delivery timing"; there was no timing. It
++assumed three ticks leave a page protected. Under eager reclaim a
++COMPRESSED page stays readable until the deferred-madvise sweeper protects
++it, so the read did not fault and the "state after read" check failed
++20/20 (reproduced at the commit before the disable; data always correct,
++and a write in the window faults and is kept). Under deferred reclaim, the
++default, the page is COMPRESSED_SHADOW and read/write after three ticks, so
++the test passed without ever exercising the fault handler: with the handler
++made to restore one corrupted byte, the old test still passed. The test now
++ticks until the page has no read permission (/proc/self/maps, or
++mach_vm_region on macOS), then requires a counted fault, byte-exact data
++and a live page; it catches that mutation in both modes.
++
++Suite 50/50 with nothing disabled, unprivileged and as root (root run on a
++2-CPU x86-64 host with 8 hugepages reserved).
++
