+From dc8c37e565711666d0d5e4b6a17b66f20e4de1b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:23:01 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(vm): 1 TiB arena ceiling; shrink instead of
+ disabling on reservation failure
+
+SMASH_VM_GIB was clamped to 64 GiB (kVmMaxPages = 16M pages). That was an
+estimate of per-page metadata cost, not a limit: the arena is a PROT_NONE
+MAP_NORESERVE reservation and its metadata is demand-paged, so an unused
+arena costs address space only (measured 23.3 MB RSS at 16, 64 and 1024
+GiB). Page indices are 32-bit, so the hard bound is 16 TiB. The ceiling is
+now kVmMaxBytes = 1 TiB; the default stays 16 GiB.
+
+A failed reservation (39-bit-VA arm64, RLIMIT_AS) used to make
+VmRegion::init return false, and smash ran with no compression at all,
+silently. It now halves the request down to the 256 MiB floor and reports
+the size it got. Measured with a 48 GiB address-space limit and
+SMASH_VM_GIB=1024: a 32 GiB arena, and a cold 16 MiB block leaves RSS
+completely; the previous library kept it 100% resident. Suite 54/54.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
