+From cab1b61cae501a43b96f6d732a5df679f96d7bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:19:06 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(vm): return freed memory to the arena: coalescing
+ free map + reclaim on exhaustion
+
+A long-running full-mode program drifted out of the compressible arena for
+good: memory past it is never compressed (and before 8ebfca0 was a
+std::bad_alloc). Two causes, both fixed:
+
+- Empty slab spans were never returned (Slab::scavenge had no callers), so
+  every page a size class had used stayed with it.
+- Freed page runs were never coalesced: 64 per-thread singly-linked lists
+  of FreeRun nodes, where a run could only serve a request no larger than
+  itself (1-page runs could not hold a 2-page span, 1 MiB runs not a
+  2 MiB block).
+
+PageRunMap (src/vm/page_run_map.h) replaces the lists: boundary tags in
+demand-paged per-page arrays, size bins with a non-empty bitmap, merging
+with both neighbours on free. Owners keep NUMA node arenas apart. When
+neither the map nor the bump pointer can serve a request, VmRegion calls
+an exhausted hook: the heap returns every slab's empty spans synchronously
+(Slab::reclaimEmptySpans, VmRegion::releasePagesNow, tryLock only), they
+coalesce, and the allocation is retried before falling back to mmap. Span
+descriptors keep their bitmap across recycling, and the descriptor free
+list is a spinlock stack instead of a Treiber stack with an ABA race.
+
+Measured, 1 GiB arena, ~70% phases freed in between: 128 B / 256 B / 1 KiB
+went from 40 / 6 / 0% in the arena to 100%, and 1 / 2 / 3 MiB blocks from
+0% to 100%. With merging disabled, or the hook not registered, the new
+test_arena_reuse fails the same six phases. test_page_run_map checks the
+map against a per-page model (284 k operations, 4,919 takes only merged
+runs can serve) and fails 21 checks with merging disabled.
+
+Returning spans eagerly on every free was tried first and made mi-stress
+~70% slower (16.9 s -> 28.7 s; isolated to trimming, not the map).
+Reclaiming on exhaustion costs nothing in steady state: mi-stress 16.7-16.9 s
+vs 16.2-16.9 s, thread churn 83-86 s vs 86 s, and 16 threads of 1-4 MiB
+blocks got faster (10.2 s vs 16.6 s). 64 threads with the hook firing
+constantly: 2.56 M allocations, 0 nulls, no deadlock.
+
+Also: smash_in_arena(ptr) diagnostic export. Suite 56/56 default,
+forced-uffd, and as root.
+
