+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:33:24 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 4/4] test(span): guard the span-descriptor free-list race that
+ cab1b61 fixed
+
+cab1b61 replaced the span-descriptor free list, a lock-free Treiber stack,
+with a spinlock stack while adding span recycling. The old stack had the
+textbook ABA race (pop reads s->next_free, then CASes the head), and it
+crashed real workloads before any of this work: a 64-thread churn stress
+segfaulted the previous library, and a targeted stress (concurrent aligned
+new/delete with cross-thread frees) crashed it 5 of 5 runs, with smash
+failing to recognise its own block on free and forwarding it to glibc
+("free(): invalid pointer") or segfaulting.
+
+Attributed, not assumed: the current code with ONLY that list reverted to
+the Treiber stack crashed 5 of 5; with the spinlock, 0 of 5. It also hits
+large-only mode (allocations over 16 KiB go through LargeAlloc): 2 of 3
+runs crashed with the old stack, 0 of 3 with the fix.
+
+New test_span_descriptor_race_{full,large_only} (64 threads, aligned
+objects in full mode, 32 KiB blocks in large-only; probabilistic, about 2
+runs in 3 with the old stack). Suite 58/58.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
