From 148ba4c1c6e3fa21827d874bb9dd6e79427ab571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:45:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(bootstrap): scale the metadata arena and never
 dereference null when it runs out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported: an app crashed at ~169 GB RSS with nothing in its logs. Every slab
span costs a Span descriptor plus a bitmap in BootstrapAlloc, which is never
freed, so that arena bounds the heap smash can manage. Fixed 16 MiB
expansions capped it at 64 MiB + 63 x 16 MiB = 1.07 GiB — roughly a 100 GB
heap of large size classes — and then allocate() returned null into code
that did not check it: a write to address 0.

Reproduced with the cap cut to 2 regions: a 16-byte-object workload
segfaulted at 0x0 after ~40 M objects.

- Regions now double (16 -> 32 -> ... -> kBootstrapMaxExpandSize = 256 MiB),
  so 64 regions reach 15.4 GiB, covering a multi-TB heap. With the cap cut
  to 6 regions, flat growth exhausts at 144 MiB and fails the workload while
  geometric gives 560 MiB and completes. test_bootstrap now fails if the
  computed capacity drops below 8 GiB.
- Bitmaps are sized per class again (bitmap_store_words). cab1b61 sized every
  bitmap for the largest span, wasting 248 B on a 16 KiB class and cutting
  the coverable heap 3x (329 GB -> 102 GB).
- Exhaustion reports itself once and fails the allocation instead of
  crashing: newSpanDescriptor, Span::init (now returns bool),
  Slab::allocateNewSpan, LargeAlloc::allocate (both sites), PageMap::ensureL2,
  Slab::pushPending, and VmRegion::queueForDecommit, whose queue entry comes
  from the same arena and now falls back to a synchronous release. With the
  arena cut to one 64 MiB region: 4/4 runs now end in std::bad_alloc with a
  message; before, 2/3 segfaulted. Each null path was found by a crash and a
  backtrace, not by reading.
- The stats line reports boot=<used>/<mapped>MiB(<regions>).

Suite 58/58 (test_malloc_numa_full failed once under parallel build load and
did not reproduce: 3/3 under deliberate load on this build and on the
previous library).

